#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_union

#% text
# `region_union(r1, r2, ...)` is the union of plane polygons (rectangles, triangles, and disks as fine polygons) as a polygon.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Several pieces give a polygon of several rings; holes give `polygon(outer -> holes)`.

#% item
# Coordinates are computed with machine numbers; exact input gives exact rationals back where they are small.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Two overlapping squares:

#% cell
region_union(rectangle([0, 0], [2, 2]), rectangle([1, 1], [3, 3]))
#% output
#= polygon([[0, 0], [2, 0], [2, 1], [3, 1], [3, 3], [1, 3], [1, 2], [0, 2]])

#% text
# Its area:

#% cell
area(region_union(rectangle([0, 0], [2, 2]), rectangle([1, 1], [3, 3])))
#% output
#= 7

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `region_intersection`, `region_difference`
